#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:4
msgid "Uniwill laptop extra features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:6
msgid ""
"On laptops manufactured by Uniwill (either directly or as ODM), the "
"``uniwill-laptop`` driver handles various platform-specific features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:10
msgid "Module Loading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:12
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver relies on a DMI table to automatically load on "
"supported devices. When using the ``force`` module parameter, this DMI check "
"will be omitted, allowing the driver to be loaded on unsupported devices for "
"testing purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:17
msgid "Hotkeys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:19
msgid ""
"Usually the FN keys work without a special driver. However as soon as the "
"``uniwill-laptop`` driver is loaded, the FN keys need to be handled "
"manually. This is done automatically by the driver itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:23
msgid "Keyboard settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:25
msgid "The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver allows the user to enable/disable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:27
msgid "the FN lock and super key of the integrated keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:28
msgid "the touchpad toggle functionality of the integrated touchpad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:30
#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:99
msgid "See Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-uniwill-laptop for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:33
msgid "Hwmon interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:35
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver supports reading of the CPU and GPU "
"temperature and supports up to two fans. Userspace applications can access "
"sensor readings over the hwmon sysfs interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:39
msgid "Platform profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:41
msgid ""
"Support for changing the platform performance mode is currently not "
"implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:44
msgid "Battery Charging Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:46
msgid ""
"Some devices do not properly implement the charging threshold interface. "
"Forcing the driver to enable access to said interface on such devices might "
"damage the battery [1]_. Because of this the driver will not enable said "
"feature even when using the ``force`` module parameter. The charging profile "
"interface will be available instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:52
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver supports controlling the battery charge limit. "
"This either happens over the standard ``charge_control_end_threshold`` or "
"``charge_types`` power supply sysfs attribute, depending on the device. When "
"using the ``charge_control_end_threshold`` sysfs attribute, all values "
"between 1 and 100 percent are supported. When using the ``charge_types`` "
"sysfs attribute, the driver supports switching between the ``Standard``, "
"``Trickle`` and ``Long Life`` profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:58
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that when using the ``charge_types`` sysfs attribute, the EC "
"firmware will hide the true charging status of the battery from the "
"operating system, potentially misleading users into thinking that the "
"charging profile does not work. Checking the ``current_now`` sysfs attribute "
"tells you the true charging status of the battery even when using the "
"``charge_types`` sysfs attribute (0 means that the battery is currently not "
"charging)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:64
msgid ""
"Additionally the driver signals the presence of battery charging issues "
"through the standard ``health`` power supply sysfs attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:67
msgid ""
"It also lets you set whether a USB-C power source should prioritise charging "
"the battery or delivering immediate power to the cpu. See Documentation/ABI/"
"testing/sysfs-driver-uniwill-laptop for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:72
msgid "Lightbar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:74
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver exposes the lightbar found on some models as a "
"standard multicolor LED class device. The default name of this LED class "
"device is ``uniwill:multicolor:status``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:77
msgid ""
"See Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-uniwill-laptop for details on how "
"to control the various animation modes of the lightbar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:81
msgid "Keyboard Backlight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:83
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver supports controlling the keyboard backlight "
"using the standard LED class interface. The default name of this LED class "
"device is ``uniwill:white:kbd_backlight`` when the keyboard backlight "
"supports only a single color, or ``uniwill:multicolor:kbd_backlight`` when "
"the keyboard backlight supports RGB colors. The maximum intensity for each "
"color channel in RGB mode is 50."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:89
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that due to hardware design choices, the driver does not "
"support the RGB value ``0x000000`` (black), instead it will fall back to "
"``0x010101`` (faint white). In order to disable the keyboard backlight, the "
"standard LED brightness setting has to be used instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:94
msgid "Configurable TGP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:96
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver allows to set the configurable TGP for devices "
"with NVIDIA GPUs that allow it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:102
msgid "AC Auto Boot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:104
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver allows the user to configure if the system "
"should automatically boot when being connected to a power source, see "
"Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-uniwill-laptop for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:109
msgid "USB Powershare"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/laptops/uniwill-laptop.rst:111
msgid ""
"The ``uniwill-laptop`` driver allows the user to configure if the system "
"should continue to provide power via the USB ports when hibernating or "
"powered off, see Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-uniwill-laptop for "
"details."
msgstr ""

